# DSA Progress Tracking

- Treat `PROGRESS.md` in the project root as the source of truth for per-question progress.
- When the learner explicitly says a problem is solved/completed, or clearly confirms the final solution works, update that question's status to **Completed**, add a brief learning note, and append a dated entry to the session log.
- When the learner reports completing practice files in a topic folder, review the files to identify each exercise and record the topic and exercises in the dated session log. Treat their explicit report that they practiced/completed them as confirmation; do not infer completion from file presence alone.
- When they are still asking for hints, debugging, or whether an approach is correct. Do not infer completion just because code was discussed or corrected.
- If the question number is unclear, record the pattern description under “Worked on in this chat — completion not confirmed”; do not guess a question number.
- Preserve prior entries. Do not mark all questions complete based only on the old grouped summary in `00-Logic-Building/readme.md`.
- After updating progress, tell the learner which question/status was recorded.

